	(text "TSSOP-16 -> DIP-16 300 mil adapter, PicoGUS THT v1.3.2. Use: U3, U4 (SN74CB3T3257) on PicoGUS THT v1.3.2.\nMapping: TSSOP pin n -> DIP pin n for every pin (net names Pn_<pin name>); nothing else in the signal path.\nBoard: 10.16 x 20.32 mm, 1 mm chamfer at the pin-1 corner = the body outline of the main-board footprint\nDIP-16_W7.62mm_TSSOP-16_Adapter (it fits that courtyard).\nAssembly: solder the TSSOP first. Then fit two 1x8 round machined pin strips from the BOTTOM (insulator under\nthe board), solder them on the top and cut the tails flush. J1 holes 1.0 mm. The round 0.47 mm pins fit\nmachined DIP sockets (On Shore SA163000) and the 1.0 mm main-board holes.\nSquare 0.64 mm header pins also fit the 1.0 mm holes, but only for soldering straight into the main board:\nnever push square pins into a machined socket."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
